{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:33:44.266Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-25T12:33:44.265Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Registry input 2026-07-25 (directed maintainer pass): pm-4k6b note (22) proposes counterfactual replay evaluation under this harness — replaying a candidate scorer against recorded request points from real sessions and comparing on whether subsequently touched items were served, at what rank, and at what token cost. It is off-policy evaluation and must be documented with its honest limit: it cannot observe what an agent would have done with items it never saw, so it bounds improvement rather than proving it, and a replay win still requires a live comparison before a default changes. Its value is filtering — rejecting most scoring proposals on recorded data rather than shipping them. Recorded here so the harness scope covers counterfactual comparison and not only graded judgments; see pm-g8t7b9 for the full ownership disposition."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:33:44.266Z"}],"before_hash":"1756ac6ddc068b04c5560d64cc962e43a7579202a49fa0a6883b2b2f4f8e200e","after_hash":"8b7c20ad08f8c937a39e8c70b57027e48b02da835afc44980932721d1961d5e0"}
{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:41:54.275Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:41:54.275Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-25T12:41:54.275Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"An evaluation mechanism must never be owned by the item whose work it evaluates. When a scoring item owns its own harness, the harness's acceptance criteria are written to be satisfiable by that scorer, and a genuinely falsifying result becomes a scope negotiation rather than a finding. Keeping the judgment corpus, the replay harness, and the counterfactual evaluator under an evaluation-owned item — with scoring items depending on them rather than containing them — is what preserves the ability to reject a scoring idea on evidence."}]}],"before_hash":"8b7c20ad08f8c937a39e8c70b57027e48b02da835afc44980932721d1961d5e0","after_hash":"9609ba2b23723009fe3b5cfd88a110e96808764f1934eb6ff504e59a59209505"}
{"ts":"2026-07-26T05:54:42.986Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","op":"update","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies/4","value":{"id":"pm-9rxu","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-07-26T05:54:42.632Z"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T05:54:42.986Z"}],"before_hash":"9609ba2b23723009fe3b5cfd88a110e96808764f1934eb6ff504e59a59209505","after_hash":"048278622a951ef918d5f5701ea7f52c20552a62f22f5c2c0b098d2a2fb27f0e","message":"Strategic reachability edge: mirror the hierarchy rung into the typed layer so every active item resolves to an outcome milestone through an explainable implements path (pm-bzmeaa invariant), which the parent chain alone cannot express because it terminates at the roadmap root rather than at an outcome"}
